# T22652 — S2166.1.10–12 — modbus — read alarm information — tb470 IE520 stack — 2026-09-29 — PASS

Verdict: PASS. Alarm #1's type, configuration and status registers were read on every stack
member and each equals the CLI: type 1 = "External PSU" (the first per-member alarm in `show
alarm facility settings`), configuration 0x0000 = no LED/relay output ("-" in the settings
table; T22654 showed the same word read 0x8000 when the CLI had the LED configured), status
FALSE on members 1 and 4 and TRUE on member 3 = `show system environment` "Power Input 1: Yes /
No / Yes". The addresses printed in the case text (0x3600–0x3602) belong to an older register
map and answer illegal-data-address on this Mapping-Version-5 DUT; the alarm block is at 0x3000
with SIX words per alarm (type, config, 3 reserved, status). Run labelled: clean.

Operator: bench-runner subagent (device-testing-61 = sentinel; Terrence away). Queue row 8,
case 6 of 6. Hand-driven: ckcon.py on /dev/u5 + mb.py (pymodbus 3.8.6) from tb470 eth1 →
stack vlan1 10.38.215.10. Full stdout 22652.out, client log mb-22652.log, driver reads3.sh.

## Case (ck.db AWPTCM-T22652)
Objective: retrieve alarm information (alarm list = `show alarm facility settings`). Steps:
1 read 0x3600 #1 Alarm Type (1 word ENUM); 2 read 0x3601 #1 Alarm Configuration (1 word HEX);
3 read 0x3602 #1 Alarm Status (1 word BOOL).
Register semantics on this DUT (measured in T22654, 22654-alarm-discovery.out: a 93-word dump
of unit 1 from 0x3000 and the CLI cross-check): per member (unit id), 6 words per alarm from
0x3000 — [type, config, 0, 0, 0, status]; type per the ART table (1 External PSU, 2 EPSR,
3 External contact input, 4 Link down, 5 Loop detect, 6 Main PSE failure, 7 PoE failure,
8 Temperature, 9 G8032, 10 UFO); config bitmap MSB-first (0x8000 = LED, 0x8000>>n = relay n);
status 0xffff = alarm condition present, 0x0000 = not. Alarm order = the CLI's per-member
order: #1 External PSU 1, #2 External PSU 2, #3..#30 Link down portN.0.1..28, #31 Temperature.

