## Reads (14:07:07–14:07:10; TX bytes in mb-22652.log)
The case's literal addresses, unit 1:
  READ 0x3600 x1 -> EXCEPTION · READ 0x3601 x1 -> EXCEPTION · READ 0x3602 x1 -> EXCEPTION
  (illegal data address, +3 on the server counter: 13 → 16) — not registers of this map.
Steps at the DUT's addresses (alarm #1 = External PSU 1):
  member 1 (unit 1):
    step 1  READ 0x3000 x1 ENUM -> words=['0x0001'] value=1        = External PSU  (CLI first row "External PSU 1")
    step 2  READ 0x3001 x1 HEX  -> words=['0x0000'] value='0000'   = no LED, no relay  (CLI Outputs "-")
    step 3  READ 0x3005 x1 BOOL -> words=['0x0000'] value=False    = PSU 1 present  (CLI Power Input 1 "Yes")
            READ 0x3002 x3 RAW  -> [0, 0, 0]                        (reserved words 2–4)
  member 3 (unit 3):
    step 1  READ 0x3000 -> 1 (External PSU)
    step 2  READ 0x3001 -> '0000'                                    (CLI "-")
    step 3  READ 0x3005 -> words=['0xffff'] value=True              = PSU 1 ABSENT  (CLI Power Input 1 "No")
  member 4 (unit 4):
    step 1  READ 0x3000 -> 1 · step 2 READ 0x3001 -> '0000' · step 3 READ 0x3005 -> False  (CLI Power Input 1 "Yes")
  unit 0: READ 0x3000 x6 -> [1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0xffff] = member 3's entry (unit 0 serves the master's block).
Consistency of the neighbouring entries (extra, same reads):
  #2 External PSU 2 (0x3006 x6): member 1 [1,0,0,0,0,0xffff] (Power Input 2 No), member 3
     [1,0,0,0,0,0] (Yes), member 4 [1,0,0,0,0,0xffff] (No) — all as the CLI.
  #3 Link down portN.0.1 (0x300c x6): [4,0,0,0,0,0xffff] on all three — port N.0.1 is an empty
     cage, link down, on every member (T22653: `show interface port1.0.1` Link is DOWN).
  #4 Link down portN.0.2 (0x3012 x6): [4,0,0,0,0,0] on all three — 1.0.2, 3.0.2, 4.0.2 are all
     linked (bench-state: to the x230 / the 4050).
  0x305a x6 -> [4,0,0,0,0,0xffff]: labelled "#31 Temperature" in the driver by a stride slip
     (3-word arithmetic); with 6-word entries 0x305a is entry #16 = Link down portN.0.14, which is
     down on every member — the value fits. The Temperature entry (#31) sits at 0x30b4 and was
     NOT read; nothing in the case needs it.
Server counters after: holding-register reads 177, illegal data address 16.

## Per-step verdict
1 PASS (type = External PSU on members 1, 3, 4) · 2 PASS (config 0x0000 = "-"; the word is
live — T22654 read 0x8000 with the CLI LED set) · 3 PASS (status = the inverse of "Power Input 1"
on each member: False/True/False for Yes/No/Yes). Note for the case owner: the AWPTCM step text
names 0x3600–0x3602; the DUT implements the alarm block at 0x3000 (map version 5), 6 words per
alarm, addressed per stack member by unit id.

